{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786750156748031002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"saintly-letterhigh-yaffle","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7612f4e5213b9f6f5e294e1ea74e8b91f4434c689f3ef549652ba46071bf0bda","event_uuid":"edd65b6e-7d71-488c-87c5-246c6aecab56","position":{"commit_sha":"beb056940ad809abccf9d9af2d0d45a36eaa7b01","position":"1786750156748031001-edd65b6e-7d71-488c-87c5-246c6aecab56"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786750156748031001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Symptom\nEvery rebar LLM operation (review-plan, verify-completion, gated close) fails with \"no AWS region could be resolved\" in any shell where only AWS_REGION is exported — even though AWS_REGION is the standard region variable set by modern AWS tooling (CLI v2 docs, SDKs) and is what operators typically export in their shell profile. Observed 2026-08-14: an operator's login shell exports AWS_REGION=us-west-2; every subagent/tool shell inherits it; rebar's bedrock provider still refuses to run until REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION or AWS_DEFAULT_REGION is manually injected per command.\n\n## Root cause (already measured and documented by rebar's own error text)\nrebar delegates region resolution entirely to botocore, and botocore 1.43.62 does not resolve a region from AWS_REGION alone (measured: AWS_DEFAULT_REGION unset + AWS_REGION set -> no region). rebar's error message documents this trap in detail instead of closing it. Resolution order today: REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION -> AWS_DEFAULT_REGION -> profile config; AWS_REGION is never consulted.\n\n## Fix\nAdd AWS_REGION to rebar's own resolution chain: REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION -> AWS_DEFAULT_REGION -> AWS_REGION -> profile/botocore default, passing the resolved value explicitly to the boto3 client (region_name=...) so botocore's quirk is irrelevant. Record the resolved source in the verdict's provider provenance exactly as REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION is today. Update the error message to list the full chain (and drop the now-moot AWS_REGION warning paragraph).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] With only AWS_REGION set (AWS_DEFAULT_REGION and REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION unset), bedrock-backed operations resolve that region and run; test pins the resolution order (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION beats AWS_DEFAULT_REGION beats AWS_REGION).\n- [ ] Resolved region + source recorded in provider provenance (test).\n- [ ] Error message on no-region-anywhere names the full chain; stale AWS_REGION-does-not-work guidance removed (doc/test).\n- [ ] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8274-6714-32b6-48be","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bedrock region resolution ignores AWS_REGION, the standard env var operators actually set","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["edd65b6e-7d71-488c-87c5-246c6aecab56"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786750156748031002,"uuid":"544ec556-5008-4c77-a41f-04e8a6682f60"}